# PART 17 — My final verdict

If I were responsible for developing Aethel OS, these would be my five biggest priorities:

| Rank | Improvement | Why |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Unified Client 360° | Makes all client information accessible in one place |
| 2 | Proper Dashboard | Gives an immediate picture of studio operations |
| 3 | Connected Finance & Ledger | Ensures financial accuracy |
| 4 | Project & Task Management | Makes actual delivery easier |
| 5 | Automation Engine | Reduces repetitive administrative work |

And there are three things I would absolutely avoid:

**1. Don't keep adding cards.**

The answer to every missing feature shouldn't be another dashboard card.

**2. Don't introduce unnecessary complexity.**

Aethel Studios is an agency. Your software should make running an agency easier, not require you to spend half your day managing the management software.

**3. Don't sacrifice functionality for aesthetics.**

Your current visual identity is already strong. The next stage should be about usability, intelligence and workflow efficiency.

